You are on a plane. 

On your knees, a briefcase. 

Inside the briefcase, some papers, all marked with the Agency's logo

The Agency is where you work. It's the European agency tasked with patrolling a securing 
the Union's external borders. It employs ten thousands people, mostly police and bureaucrats
like yourself, and consts more than a billion euros each year. The headquarters are in
a glass skyscraper in Warsaw. You were there this morning. 

Now you're on a plane.

